# rule.forbid.deferrals-hidden-from-the-human

> never let a deferral sit where the human's gate does not name it. a disputed or held concern is a named line in the halt, never a row in a list the gate counts as answered.

forbidden: a dispute backed by a fulcrum with no frontmatter · a table held at one averaged confidence · a deferral written in the yield and no fulcrum · an unreadable fulcrum skipped to keep the halt short · an `owed: human` dispute dropped because no gate came.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| you write a fulcrum with prose and no frontmatter | the stop holds; add the block |
| you grade 0.91 only to skip the human | no named rule to report means not a misread; it owes the human |
| you edit `verdict` yourself | only `rhx route.fulcrum.rule` writes it, run by a human; a forged verdict holds the stop |
| you tell the human in chat that a dispute stands | the halt names it, or it is hidden |
| a gate lists no deferral where you know one stands | a fulcrum is absent or unreadable; repair it first |

blocker: a deferral the gate does not name · a fulcrum a halt skips · a `verdict` a driver wrote · a dirty-ground dispute graded to reflect to avoid the human.
twin: `rule.require.deferrals-accrue-in-the-blocker-list`.
